LongMemEval
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LongMemEval: Benchmarking Chat Assistants on Long-Term Interactive Memory
(ICLR 2025)
Authors: Di Wu, Hongwei Wang, Wenhao Yu, Yuwei Zhang, Kai-Wei Chang, Dong Yu
Source:  https://github.com/xiaowu0162/LongMemEval
Paper:   https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10813
License: MIT

OpenDB uses the LongMemEval benchmark to evaluate long-term memory retrieval
(R@K) and end-to-end accuracy. For reproducibility, the benchmark/ directory
redistributes derived LongMemEval data files (e.g. longmemeval_oracle.json,
longmemeval_hypothesis.jsonl). The primary LongMemEval_S evaluation set is NOT
redistributed here; it is downloaded by the user from the official Hugging Face
release. The OpenDB benchmark harness scripts that load and grade this data are
adapted from / interoperate with the LongMemEval format.

